<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$31 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$31 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two unlisted Australian commercial paper issuers held promissory note tenders totalling A$31 million on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Government-owned telecoms group Telstra Corp made the larger issue of the two, selling A$20 million worth of one-month paper.</p>
<p>The bank bill market has strengthened over the morning, taking their lead from firmer U.S. Treasuries which responded favourably to U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's economic outlook speech to the U.S. Senate Budget Committee.</p>
<p>But dealers said turnover remained slight.</p>
<p>At 11.50 a.m. (0050 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.37, down three points on the day.</p>
